{"insertText":{"location":{"index":144719,"tabId":"t.l5c18frq5wuo"},"text":"\nTable XI compares the BO-selected SwinFusion++ with the fixed-recipe encoders, and Table XII compares it with the fixed-recipe SwinFusion++. Because only SwinFusion++ received a hyperparameter search, Table XI measures configured-system performance with unequal optimization effort and is not evidence about the architecture itself."}},
{"updateParagraphStyle":{"range":{"startIndex":144720,"endIndex":145053,"tabId":"t.l5c18frq5wuo"},"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","alignment":"JUSTIFIED","lineSpacing":200,"indentFirstLine":{"magnitude":36,"unit":"PT"},"spaceAbove":{"magnitude":0,"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"magnitude":0,"unit":"PT"},"keepWithNext":false},"fields":"namedStyleType,alignment,lineSpacing,indentFirstLine,spaceAbove,spaceBelow,keepWithNext"}},
{"updateTextStyle":{"range":{"startIndex":144720,"endIndex":145052,"tabId":"t.l5c18frq5wuo"},"textStyle":{"fontSize":{"magnitude":12,"unit":"PT"}},"fields":"bold,italic,underline,backgroundColor,fontSize"}},
{"updateTextStyle":{"range":{"startIndex":145052,"endIndex":145053,"tabId":"t.l5c18frq5wuo"},"textStyle":{"fontSize":{"magnitude":12,"unit":"PT"}},"fields":"bold,italic,underline,backgroundColor,fontSize"}},
{"insertText":{"location":{"index":144719,"tabId":"t.l5c18frq5wuo"},"text":"\nBayesian-Optimized Configuration"}},
{"updateParagraphStyle":{"range":{"startIndex":144720,"endIndex":144753,"tabId":"t.l5c18frq5wuo"},"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","alignment":"JUSTIFIED","lineSpacing":200,"indentFirstLine":{"magnitude":0,"unit":"PT"},"spaceAbove":{"magnitude":0,"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"magnitude":0,"unit":"PT"},"keepWithNext":true},"fields":"namedStyleType,alignment,lineSpacing,indentFirstLine,spaceAbove,spaceBelow,keepWithNext"}},
{"updateTextStyle":{"range":{"startIndex":144720,"endIndex":144752,"tabId":"t.l5c18frq5wuo"},"textStyle":{"fontSize":{"magnitude":12,"unit":"PT"},"bold":true},"fields":"bold,italic,underline,backgroundColor,fontSize"}},
{"updateTextStyle":{"range":{"startIndex":144752,"endIndex":144753,"tabId":"t.l5c18frq5wuo"},"textStyle":{"fontSize":{"magnitude":12,"unit":"PT"},"bold":true},"fields":"bold,italic,underline,backgroundColor,fontSize"}},
{"insertText":{"location":{"index":144719,"tabId":"t.l5c18frq5wuo"},"text":"\nThe ROC curves illustrate the split between ROC-AUC and accuracy. Outside FF++ C23 → C40, where ROC-AUC stayed near or above 0.8, the curves show that the ranking of fake above real videos was largely retained, but the frozen operating point sat in the low-recall part of the curve. Moving it would require target labels, which the frozen-transfer design excludes. Where ROC-AUC was near 0.5, as from DeeperForensics-1.0 to Celeb-DF v2, the ranking itself was close to chance, so the problem was not only the threshold. For all three models, the frozen screening label on an unseen dataset is therefore much less informative than the ranking results suggest."}},
{"updateParagraphStyle":{"range":{"startIndex":144720,"endIndex":145379,"tabId":"t.l5c18frq5wuo"},"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","alignment":"JUSTIFIED","lineSpacing":200,"indentFirstLine":{"magnitude":36,"unit":"PT"},"spaceAbove":{"magnitude":0,"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"magnitude":0,"unit":"PT"},"keepWithNext":false},"fields":"namedStyleType,alignment,lineSpacing,indentFirstLine,spaceAbove,spaceBelow,keepWithNext"}},
{"updateTextStyle":{"range":{"startIndex":144720,"endIndex":145378,"tabId":"t.l5c18frq5wuo"},"textStyle":{"fontSize":{"magnitude":12,"unit":"PT"}},"fields":"bold,italic,underline,backgroundColor,fontSize"}},
{"updateTextStyle":{"range":{"startIndex":145378,"endIndex":145379,"tabId":"t.l5c18frq5wuo"},"textStyle":{"fontSize":{"magnitude":12,"unit":"PT"}},"fields":"bold,italic,underline,backgroundColor,fontSize"}},
{"insertText":{"location":{"index":144719,"tabId":"t.l5c18frq5wuo"},"text":"\nSwinFusion++ did not have the highest accuracy, recall, or F1-score in any of the nine directions (point estimates; several margins were one or two videos). From FF++ C23, its high precision and specificity reflect that it made the fewest positive calls of the three models (114, 458, and 8 on C40, Celeb-DF v2, and DeeperForensics-1.0); from the other two sources, Swin-B made the fewest or as few as any other model. From FF++ C23 to Celeb-DF v2, for example, SwinFusion++ raised only six false alarms among 135 real videos (specificity 95.56%) but detected 53.62% of the fake videos, and its accuracy (59.41%) was lower than that of Swin-B (67.48%) and Video Swin-B (66.46%), although the three ROC-AUC values did not differ detectably. In the supplementary paired intervals (Table J2), its transfer accuracy was lower than an encoder’s in 6 of 18 comparisons (both encoders from FF++ C23 to C40 and to Celeb-DF v2; Video Swin-B from FF++ C23 to DeeperForensics-1.0 and from Celeb-DF v2 to C23) and higher in 2 (Swin-B from Celeb-DF v2 to C23 and to DeeperForensics-1.0)."}},
{"updateParagraphStyle":{"range":{"startIndex":144720,"endIndex":145795,"tabId":"t.l5c18frq5wuo"},"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","alignment":"JUSTIFIED","lineSpacing":200,"indentFirstLine":{"magnitude":36,"unit":"PT"},"spaceAbove":{"magnitude":0,"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"magnitude":0,"unit":"PT"},"keepWithNext":false},"fields":"namedStyleType,alignment,lineSpacing,indentFirstLine,spaceAbove,spaceBelow,keepWithNext"}},
{"updateTextStyle":{"range":{"startIndex":144720,"endIndex":145794,"tabId":"t.l5c18frq5wuo"},"textStyle":{"fontSize":{"magnitude":12,"unit":"PT"}},"fields":"bold,italic,underline,backgroundColor,fontSize"}},
{"updateTextStyle":{"range":{"startIndex":145794,"endIndex":145795,"tabId":"t.l5c18frq5wuo"},"textStyle":{"fontSize":{"magnitude":12,"unit":"PT"}},"fields":"bold,italic,underline,backgroundColor,fontSize"}},
{"insertText":{"location":{"index":144719,"tabId":"t.l5c18frq5wuo"},"text":"\nAt the frozen source thresholds, every model became conservative on the target data. Specificity stayed between 91.11% and 100.00%, while recall was below 64% in every direction except FF++ C23 → C40 (79.29% to 87.14%). From the Celeb-DF v2 and DeeperForensics-1.0 sources, no model flagged more than 60 test videos as fake, so accuracy in those directions mainly reflects the share of real videos. From DeeperForensics-1.0 to Celeb-DF v2, where 86.20% of the test videos are fake, accuracy was only 13.80% to 15.24%, close to the 13.80% obtained by calling every video real."}},
